0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Motorola 6809
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-24).
0000                             ;  Follows the design of the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two switches, in the EQU lines below (CPM is always 0: the 6809 has no
0000                             ;  CP/M; the line is kept only so that build.sh works):
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: an unchecked build checks nothing)
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build: variables start at 0, words start
0000                             ;                 undefined, and every error in the spec's table stops the
0000                             ;                 program with the four-line report, then goes to EXIT:
0000                             ;                   Err X @ line,col
0000                             ;                   <up to 16 characters of the text at the place>
0000                             ;                   Stk n: ... v v v      (n = depth, then the top 8 values)
0000                             ;                   Rtn n
0000                             ;                 S/s data stack over/underflow, R/r return stack over/
0000                             ;                 underflow, H heap, O store outside the program's space,
0000                             ;                 W bad character after [, U undefined word, Q no closing
0000                             ;                 quote, X reserved byte, Z divide by zero, N unbalanced or
0000                             ;                 mismatched brackets, B Ctrl-C.
0000                             ;    ANSI     what the console escapes of "$" (/00bbIC8= /| /` /~) do:
0000                             ;             1 = send ANSI (VT100) sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = call the machine's own routines CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR and
0000                             ;                 CONAT (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In both builds Ctrl-C stops a running program (the unchecked build goes
0000                             ;  to EXIT without a word): see the console layer below for the rules, the
0000                             ;  held key and the break-off cell at 827Bh.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, M6809 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; always 0 (no CP/M on the 6809)
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console escapes send ANSI sequences
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    Y    IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    U    the data stack pointer. The stack grows down and U points at the
0000                             ;         top cell (TOS); nothing is cached in a register, because every
0000                             ;         dispatch needs A, B and X as scratch. Cells are big-endian here.
0000                             ;         (Only the stacks are big-endian: cells in RAM that the program can
0000                             ;         see - variables, the heap pointer, anything @ and ! reach - are
0000                             ;         little-endian, as the spec says, so @ and ! swap the bytes.)
0000                             ;    S    the return stack. A word call is a plain push of Y. Entries are
0000                             ;         2 bytes, big-endian. Handlers are called with JSR, so the return
0000                             ;         address of the dispatcher is on top of S while a handler runs.
0000                             ;    DP   the letter page, so the letter-page variables below cost 2-byte
0000                             ;         direct addressing. Nothing else may change DP.
0000                             ;    A B X are scratch. Every handler is entered by JSR and ends in RTS (one
0000                             ;    byte). A handler that pushes or pops the return stack first pulls the
0000                             ;    dispatcher's return address into X (PULS X) and ends with JMP ,X.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch (unchecked build). PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character:
0000                             ;  the low byte of the handler's distance from PTAB. The handlers of the last
0000                             ;  characters (in code order) start within 256 bytes after PTAB, the handlers
0000                             ;  of the first NPG1 characters in the 256 bytes after that. The assembler
0000                             ;  works NPG1 out from where five handlers landed, and testing/chktab09.py
0000                             ;  checks the layout. The checked build is bigger than that reach, so its
0000                             ;  table holds whole addresses instead.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM areas:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    8000h-80FFh  return stack (S); empty = 8100h. Unchecked: 127 entries.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 112 entries (S down to 8020h); the 32 bytes below
0000                             ;                 are a guard band for what a handler and an interrupt push
0000                             ;                 on top of a full stack before the check runs.
0000                             ;    8100h-81FFh  data stack (U). Unchecked: 127 cells, empty = 8200h.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 126 cells (U from 81FCh, empty, down to 8100h):
0000                             ;                 the 4 bytes above are a guard band, so a handler that runs
0000                             ;                 on an empty stack writes there and not on the letter
0000                             ;                 cells. A push past the last cell lands on the return
0000                             ;                 stack's bottom entry (80FEh), and the program stops with S
0000                             ;                 before anything reads it.
0000                             ;    8200h-82FFh  letter page (LET): A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h
0000                             ;                 (a word cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the
0000                             ;                 heap pointer at +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the
0000                             ;                 gaps, and the -n? line buffer at +80h..+FFh. The break-off
0000                             ;                 cell is at +7Bh (827Bh); +7Ah is free.
0000                             ;    8300h-       PROG, the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts
0000                             ;                 after the NUL and grows to HEAPLIM*256 (F000h)
0000                             ;    F000h-       this image (ROM). The reset vector (FFFEh) must point to
0000                             ;                 `start` (see the listing); the image does not contain it.
0000                             ;    FF03h-FF17h  the console routines (CONOUT, KEY, and with ANSI = 0
0000                             ;                 CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR, CONAT) and EXIT are supplied by
0000                             ;                 the system and need no space here.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range LET..HEAPLIM*256.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (end the
0000                             ;   routine with TSTA / RTS, or a plain LDA).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   Both are called with JSR. They may change A and CC and must preserve
0000                             ;   B, X, Y, U and DP.
0000                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the console escapes of "$" call these as subroutines (each
                                 ; ends with RTS). All four may change A, B, X and CC, and must keep Y, U
                                 ; and DP.
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Ch   ; /{  clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; /}  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF12h   ; /| and /`  show the cursor if A is not 0, hide
                                 ;     it if A = 0
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF15h   ; /~  the cursor to row X, column D, both counted
                                 ;     from 0
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                             ; (the checked startup counts on it being
0000                             ; the page after LETPAGE)
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   20   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ; for your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (direct-page offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer (little-endian)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   34h   ; gap after Z: a key held back by the break check
0000                COUNT:    EQU   35h   ; the break check's countdown (1 look in 256)
0000                AT:       EQU   36h   ; checked: the address of the character being
0000                             ;   run (big-endian), the place an error reports
0000                PEND:     EQU   38h   ; checked: the program's end, the first byte
0000                             ;   after its NUL (big-endian): the heap's floor
0000                SSAV:     EQU   3Ah   ; checked: S as each character starts (big-
0000                             ;   endian): the return stack an error reports
0000                PSAV:     EQU   3Ch   ; checked: the address "$" prints from (big-
0000                             ;   endian), put back on the stack for a Q
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   7Bh   ; the break-off cell (827Bh, z9+): 0 = the
0000                             ;   break key is on
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty return stack
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+20h   ; checked: S may go no lower between characters
0000                RSREP:    EQU   RSTOP-16   ; checked: S while the error report runs
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+100h-4*CHECKED   ; empty data stack (a guard if checked)
0000                DSLIM:    EQU   DSPAGE*256   ; checked: U may go no lower between characters
F000                          .ORG   0F000h   
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ;  Startup
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000   10 CE 81 00  START:    LDS   #RSTOP   
F004   CE 82 00               LDU   #DSTOP   
F007   86 82                  LDA   #LETPAGE   
F009   1F 8B                  TFR   A,DP   
F00B                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Zero the whole letter page: every variable starts at 0, every word
                                 ; cell at 0 (undefined: a call stops with U), and so do the
                                 ; interpreter's own cells in the gaps (KEYBUF and the rest). A is
                                 ; still LETPAGE; 256 rounds leave X at the next page, PROG.
                              CLRB      
                              TFR   D,X   
                    SZ:       CLR   ,X+   
                              DECB      
                              BNE   sz   
F00B                          ENDIF      
F00B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F00B   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   ; no key held
F00D   0F 7B                  CLR   <BRKOFF   ; the break key is on
F00F   8E 83 00               LDX   #PROG   
F012                          ENDIF      
F012   1F 12                  TFR   X,Y   ; the reading position; the heap starts
F014   A6 80        SC:       LDA   ,X+   ;   after the program's NUL
F016   26 FC                  BNE   sc   
F018   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F01A   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   ; (little-endian)
F01C   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F01E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STX   <PEND   ; the heap may never go below this
F01E                          ENDIF      
F01E                             ; =============================================================================
F01E                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
F01E                             ; 
F01E                             ;    00h          end of program
F01E                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh       ignored (control, space, DEL)
F01E                             ;    80h-FFh      reserved: ignored, or X in the checked build
F01E                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
F01E                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
F01E                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
F01E                             ;    the rest     punctuation: JSR through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
F01E                             ; =============================================================================
F01E                NEXT:        
F01E                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler:
                                 ; the pointer minus its limit, taken as unsigned, must be no more
                                 ; than the stack's size. Below the limit (an overflow) it wraps to
                                 ; FFxxh, and the compare leaves N set; above the empty point (an
                                 ; underflow) it is just over the size, and N is clear.
                              LEAX   (0-DSLIM)&0FFFFh,U   
                              CMPX   #DSTOP-DSLIM   
                              BHI   e_ds   
                              LEAX   (0-RSLIM)&0FFFFh,S   
                              CMPX   #RSTOP-RSLIM   
                              BHI   e_rs   
                              STY   <AT   ; the place, should this character fail
                              STS   <SSAV   ; and the return stack, as it is now
F01E                          ENDIF      
F01E   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F020   27 50                  BEQ   fin   ; NUL ends the program
F022   80 21                  SUBA   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
F024   25 F8                  BLO   next   ; 01h-20h ignored
F026   81 0F                  CMPA   #0Fh   
F028   25 20                  BLO   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
F02A   81 19                  CMPA   #19h   
F02C   25 2A                  BLO   digit   ; 30h-39h
F02E   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F030   25 16                  BLO   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h: A = 19h-1Fh
F032   80 20                  SUBA   #20h   ; A = c - 41h
F034   81 1A                  CMPA   #1Ah   
F036   25 2C                  BLO   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
F038   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F03A   25 0A                  BLO   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
F03C   81 3A                  CMPA   #3Ah   
F03E   25 1E                  BLO   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
F040   81 3E                  CMPA   #3Eh   
F042                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F042   24 DA                  BHS   next   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
F044                          ENDIF      
F044                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   next   ; 7Fh (DEL): ignored
                              BHI   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
F044                          ENDIF      
F044   80 1A                  SUBA   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
F046   8B 06        P5B:      ADDA   #6   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
F048   80 0A        P3A:      SUBA   #0Ah   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
F04A                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index.
F04A   8E F0 ED     PUNCT:    LDX   #PTAB   
F04D                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F04D                             ; The handler is at PTAB + D, where B is the table byte and A is 1
F04D                             ; for the first NPG1 characters, 0 for the rest.
F04D   E6 86                  LDB   A,X   
F04F   81 14                  CMPA   #NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
F051   86 00                  LDA   #0   ; (leaves the carry alone)
F053   49                     ROLA      
F054   AD 8B                  JSR   D,X   ; the handler ends in RTS
F056                          ENDIF      
F056                          IF   CHECKED   
                              ASLA      ; the table holds whole addresses
                              JSR   [A,X]   
F056                          ENDIF      
F056   20 C6                  BRA   next   
F058                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
F058   31 3F        DIGIT:    LEAY   -1,Y   
F05A   8D 27                  BSR   rdnum   
F05C   20 C0                  BRA   next   
F05E                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
F05E   8D 15        LOWER:    BSR   cellx   
F060   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F062   20 BA                  BRA   next   
F064                             ; A-Z: call the word. The IP (the address after the letter) goes on the
F064                             ; return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
F064                             ; Checked: a cell still 0 (high byte 0) was never defined, since every
F064                             ; address in the program's space is 8200h or more. The call has not been
F064                             ; made yet, so the report shows the stacks as they were.
F064   8D 0F        UPPER:    BSR   cellx   
F066   E6 84                  LDB   ,X   
F068   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F06A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   e_undef   
F06A                          ENDIF      
F06A   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F06C   1F 02                  TFR   D,Y   
F06E   8D 30                  BSR   pollk   ; the break check, at every word call
F070   20 AC                  BRA   next   
F072                             ; =============================================================================
F072                             ;  Checked build: the error entries.
F072                             ; 
F072                             ;  Each entry loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside a 3-byte
F072                             ;  CMPX # (the 8Ch), so that a run of them falls through to one place. The
F072                             ;  place an error reports is the address in AT, which the inner loop sets to
F072                             ;  each character before it runs it; the one error that reports another
F072                             ;  place (W, at the character after the [) changes AT before it comes.
F072                             ; 
F072                             ;  The report counts the return stack from SSAV, which the inner loop sets
F072                             ;  to S before each character, so an error may come from any depth of
F072                             ;  calls: a handler, chkst under one, or ctlc under "?" or the break check.
F072                             ;  (An r sets SSAV to the empty stack.) The inner loop's own entries are
F072                             ;  here, where its short branches reach them; those reached from a handler
F072                             ;  are after h_cstore, just ahead of the report.
F072                             ; =============================================================================
F072                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; ---- reached from the inner loop -------------------------------------------
                                 ; The stack checks branch here with N set for an overflow (the pointer is
                                 ; below its limit) and clear for an underflow. After an underflow that stack
                                 ; counts as empty.
                    E_DS:     BMI   e_S   
                              LDU   #DSTOP   ; s
                              LDA   #"s"   
                              BRA   eall   
                    E_RS:     BMI   e_R   
                              LDX   #RSTOP   ; r
                              STX   <SSAV   
                              LDA   #"r"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_S:      LDA   #"S"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_R:      LDA   #"R"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte (80h-FFh) outside a string
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C (from ctlc, at any depth)
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_UNDEF:   LDA   #"U"   ; a word never defined (its cell is still 0)
                    EALL:     JMP   error   
F072                          ENDIF      
F072   7E FF 09     FIN:      JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
F075                             ; cellx: A = letter index (0-25, or 32-57 for lowercase) -> X = cell address
F075   48           CELLX:    ASLA      
F076   8E 82 00               LDX   #LET   
F079   30 86                  LEAX   A,X   
F07B   39                     RTS      
F07C                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is set if it is a digit
F07C   A6 A4        ISDIG:    LDA   ,Y   
F07E   80 30                  SUBA   #"0"   
F080   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F082   39           AB9:      RTS      
F083                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP and push the value; IP is left on the
F083                             ; first non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says. The running
F083                             ; value lives in the new top cell: V = V*10 + digit.
F083   4F           RDNUM:    CLRA      
F084   5F                     CLRB      
F085   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F087   8D F3        RD1:      BSR   isdig   
F089   24 F7                  BHS   ab9   
F08B   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F08D   58                     ASLB      
F08E   49                     ROLA      
F08F   58                     ASLB      
F090   49                     ROLA      
F091   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   ; 5V
F093   58                     ASLB      
F094   49                     ROLA      ; 10V
F095   EB A0                  ADDB   ,Y+   ; and the digit, read again
F097   89 00                  ADCA   #0   
F099   83 00 30               SUBD   #30h   ; minus "0" (asm80 would put a quoted "0"
F09C                             ;   in the high byte of a 16-bit operand)
F09C   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F09E   20 E7                  BRA   rd1   
F0A0                             ; =============================================================================
F0A0                             ;  Console layer: the break key. A running program reads the keyboard only
F0A0                             ;  through pollk and getk, which between them give the break key its rules:
F0A0                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program;
F0A0                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
F0A0                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
F0A0                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
F0A0                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
F0A0                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
F0A0                             ;  On a break the unchecked build ends without a word (EXIT); the checked
F0A0                             ;  one reports B. All three keep B, X, Y and U.
F0A0                             ; =============================================================================
F0A0                             ; pollk: the break check, at every word call and every true ")" loop-back.
F0A0                             ; It looks at the keyboard only once in 256 calls.
F0A0   0A 35        POLLK:    DEC   <COUNT   
F0A2   26 37                  BNE   cc9   
F0A4   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F0A7   27 32                  BEQ   cc9   ; no key
F0A9   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
F0AB   20 0C                  BRA   ctlc   
F0AD                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 with the zero flag set if there is none.
F0AD   96 34        GETK:     LDA   <KEYBUF   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
F0AF   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   ;   the buffer (it has been through ctlc)
F0B1   4D                     TSTA      
F0B2   26 27                  BNE   cc9   
F0B4   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F0B7   27 22                  BEQ   cc9   
F0B9                             ; ctlc: a key has been read. If it is Ctrl-C and the break key is on, that
F0B9                             ; is the end. If the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one
F0B9                             ; more key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the
F0B9                             ; newest wins), and the Ctrl-C goes on: A = 3, zero flag clear.
F0B9   81 03        CTLC:     CMPA   #3   
F0BB   26 1E                  BNE   cc9   
F0BD   0D 7B                  TST   <BRKOFF   
F0BF   27 B1                  BEQ   brk   
F0C1   34 10                  PSHS   X   
F0C3   8E 13 88               LDX   #250*MSLOOP   
F0C6   BD FF 06     CC1:      JSR   KEY   
F0C9   26 06                  BNE   cc2   
F0CB   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F0CD   26 F7                  BNE   cc1   
F0CF   20 06                  BRA   cc3   
F0D1   81 03        CC2:      CMPA   #3   
F0D3   27 9D                  BEQ   brk   
F0D5   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   
F0D7   86 03        CC3:      LDA   #3   
F0D9   35 10                  PULS   X   
F0DB   39           CC9:      RTS      
F0DC                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0DC                BRK:      EQU   fin   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
F0DC                          ENDIF      
F0DC                          IF   CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B (the report
F0DC                          ENDIF      ;   takes S from SSAV, so the depth of the
F0DC                             ;   calls here doesn't matter)
F0DC                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F0DC                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F0DC                             ; return with the carry clear.
F0DC                             ; (In the unchecked build it is here, ahead of the table, to leave room in
F0DC                             ; the two ranges after it; the checked build has it next to the grave.)
F0DC                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0DC   8D 9E        HEXC:     BSR   isdig   
F0DE   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F0E0   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F0E2   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F0E4   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F0E6   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F0E8   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F0EA   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F0EC   39           HV9:      RTS      
F0ED                          ENDIF      
F0ED                             ; =============================================================================
F0ED                             ;  Dispatch table, in code order.
F0ED                             ; 
F0ED                             ;  Unchecked build: one byte per character, the low byte of the handler's
F0ED                             ;  distance from PTAB. NPG1 is how many characters, from the start, have
F0ED                             ;  handlers more than 255 bytes past PTAB. ] \ [ @ ? sit where the two ranges
F0ED                             ;  meet (in falling code order for this), and which side each lands on is
F0ED                             ;  worked out here. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it
F0ED                             ;  stores a value.)
F0ED                             ; 
F0ED                             ;  Checked build: it has more code than the two ranges hold, so its table
F0ED                             ;  holds whole addresses and there are no rules about where handlers go.
F0ED                             ; =============================================================================
F0ED                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0ED                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-PTAB)/256   ; 0 = first range, 1 = second
F0ED                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-PTAB)/256   
F0ED                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-PTAB)/256   
F0ED                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-PTAB)/256   
F0ED                PGKEY:    EQU   (h_key-PTAB)/256   
F0ED                NPG1:     EQU   20 + PGKEY + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
F0ED                          ENDIF      
F0ED                PTAB:        
F0ED                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F0ED   A4                     FCB   (h_store-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; !
F0EE   1D                     FCB   (h_str-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; "
F0EF   B2                     FCB   (h_num-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; #
F0F0   F6                     FCB   (h_print-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; $
F0F1   77                     FCB   (h_swap-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; %
F0F2   8A                     FCB   (h_and-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; &
F0F3   83                     FCB   (h_emit-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; '
F0F4   13                     FCB   (h_open-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; (
F0F5   35                     FCB   (h_close-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; )
F0F6   41                     FCB   (h_mul-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; *
F0F7   92                     FCB   (h_add-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; +
F0F8   2D                     FCB   (h_cfetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ,
F0F9   99                     FCB   (h_sub-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; -
F0FA   AB                     FCB   (h_cstore-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; .
F0FB   D6                     FCB   (h_div-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; /
F0FC   7E                     FCB   (h_dup-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; :
F0FD   87                     FCB   (h_drop-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ;
F0FE   5F                     FCB   (h_lt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; <
F0FF   6B                     FCB   (h_eq-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; =
F100   5D                     FCB   (h_gt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; >
F101   C5                     FCB   (h_key-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ?
F102   BF                     FCB   (h_fetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; @
F103   84                     FCB   (h_def-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; [
F104   77                     FCB   (h_break-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; \
F105   73                     FCB   (h_ret-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ]
F106   28                     FCB   (h_xor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ^
F107   44                     FCB   (h_alloc-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; _
F108   53                     FCB   (h_grave-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; `
F109   36                     FCB   (h_tor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; {
F10A   20                     FCB   (h_or-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; |
F10B   3E                     FCB   (h_fromr-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; }
F10C   31                     FCB   (h_not-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ~
F10D                          ENDIF      
F10D                          IF   CHECKED   
                              FDB   h_store   ; !
                              FDB   h_str   ; "
                              FDB   h_num   ; #
                              FDB   h_print   ; $
                              FDB   h_swap   ; %
                              FDB   h_and   ; &
                              FDB   h_emit   ; '
                              FDB   h_open   ; (
                              FDB   h_close   ; )
                              FDB   h_mul   ; *
                              FDB   h_add   ; +
                              FDB   h_cfetch   ; ,
                              FDB   h_sub   ; -
                              FDB   h_cstore   ; .
                              FDB   h_div   ; /
                              FDB   h_dup   ; :
                              FDB   h_drop   ; ;
                              FDB   h_lt   ; <
                              FDB   h_eq   ; =
                              FDB   h_gt   ; >
                              FDB   h_key   ; ?
                              FDB   h_fetch   ; @
                              FDB   h_def   ; [
                              FDB   h_break   ; \
                              FDB   h_ret   ; ]
                              FDB   h_xor   ; ^
                              FDB   h_alloc   ; _
                              FDB   h_grave   ; `
                              FDB   h_tor   ; {
                              FDB   h_or   ; |
                              FDB   h_fromr   ; }
                              FDB   h_not   ; ~
F10D                          ENDIF      
F10D                PTABEND:      
F10D                             ; =============================================================================
F10D                             ;  Handlers that must start in the first range (within 255 bytes of PTAB)
F10D                             ;  in the unchecked build: ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~
F10D                             ; =============================================================================
F10D   EC C1        H_OR:     LDD   ,U++   
F10F   AA C4                  ORA   ,U   
F111   EA 41                  ORB   1,U   
F113   20 06                  BRA   st0   
F115   EC C1        H_XOR:    LDD   ,U++   
F117   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F119   E8 41                  EORB   1,U   
F11B   ED C4        ST0:      STD   ,U   
F11D   39                     RTS      
F11E   63 C4        H_NOT:    COM   ,U   
F120   63 41                  COM   1,U   
F122   39                     RTS      
F123                             ; "{" ( n -- ) R: ( -- n )     The dispatcher's return address comes off the
F123                             ; return stack first (PULS X) and is jumped to at the end.
F123   35 10        H_TOR:    PULS   X   
F125   37 06                  PULU   D   
F127   34 06                  PSHS   D   
F129   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F12B                             ; "}" ( -- n ) R: ( n -- )    The dispatcher's return address comes off
F12B                             ; into D and the entry under it into X; D is then jumped to.
F12B   35 16        H_FROMR:   PULS   D,X   
F12D   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F12F   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   
F131                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n (signed: a 16-bit add);
F131                             ; TOS is the old pointer.
F131                             ; Checked: the new top must be at least the program's end (PEND) and below
F131                             ; the limit page. That also catches an add that wraps: the top is always
F131                             ; 8301h-EFFFh and n is -32768..32767, so a sum that carries past FFFFh
F131                             ; lands below 7000h, and one that borrows can't happen.
F131   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
F133   96 7D                  LDA   <HEAP+1   
F135   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   ; the old pointer
F137   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F139                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CMPD   <PEND   
                              BLO   ah9   ; below the program's end
                              CMPA   #HEAPLIM   
                              BLO   ah1   ; the new top must stay below the limit page
                    AH9:      LDA   #"H"   
                              BRA   ejmp   ; (with [ below)
                    AH1:         
F139                          ENDIF      
F139   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   
F13B   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F13D   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F13F   39                     RTS      
F140                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
F140                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
F140                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS (39h) is
F140                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
F140                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
F140                             ; code is entered by JSR (the dispatcher's own), with the address already
F140                             ; popped: U points at the top data cell (big-endian, 2 bytes, stack grows
F140                             ; down) and the return address is on top of S. The code may pop and push
F140                             ; data cells by changing U; on return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F140                             ; keep Y (the interpreter's reading position), DP and S (balanced), and
F140                             ; return with RTS. A, B, X, CC may change.
F140                             ; Neither the loader's stores nor the code are checked, in either build.
F140   8D 9A        H_GRAVE:   BSR   hexc   ; the digit after the grave, if any
F142   24 1A                  BCC   exec   
F144   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   
F146   C6 10        HX1:      LDB   #16   
F148   3D                     MUL      ; B = the digit, moved up to the high half
F149   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; (an odd digit is overwritten by the RTS)
F14B   8D 8F                  BSR   hexc   
F14D   24 08                  BCC   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
F14F   AA 84                  ORA   ,X   
F151   A7 80                  STA   ,X+   
F153   8D 87                  BSR   hexc   
F155   25 EF                  BCS   hx1   
F157   86 39        HX2:      LDA   #39h   ; RTS
F159   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F15B   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F15D   39                     RTS      
F15E   37 80        EXEC:     PULU   PC   ; jump to it: the code's RTS returns to the
F160                             ;   dispatcher
F160                          IF   CHECKED   
                    HEXC:     JSR   isdig   
                              BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
                              ANDA   #0DFh   
                              SUBA   #11h   
                              CMPA   #6   
                              BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
                              SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
                    HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
                    HV9:      RTS      
F160                          ENDIF      
F160                             ; ---- where the two ranges meet ---------------------------------------------
F160                             ; The first range ends somewhere among the next five handlers, ] \ [ @ ?
F160                             ; (they are in falling code order for this): NPG1 follows. Every handler
F160                             ; below them must start in the second range, and every one above in the
F160                             ; first.
F160                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. (PULS X,Y: the dispatcher's
F160                             ; return address into X, then the saved IP into Y.)
F160   35 30        H_RET:    PULS   X,Y   
F162   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F164                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
F164                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
F164   EC C1        H_BREAK:   LDD   ,U++   
F166   27 40                  BEQ   sk9   ; false: nothing to do
F168   8D 1F                  BSR   skip   
F16A   4D                     TSTA      ; skip returns 0 for ")"
F16B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBMI   fin   ; (and FFh for the NUL: the program ends)
F16B                          ENDIF      
F16B   26 F3                  BNE   h_ret   
F16D   35 16        RDROP:    PULS   D,X   ; the return address and the block start
F16F   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   ; back to the dispatcher
F171                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
F171                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
F171                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
F171                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
F171                             ; checked build stops on it.)
F171                          IF   CHECKED   
                    DEF1:     CMPA   #" "-"A"+256   
                              BEQ   def2   
                              LEAY   -1,Y   ; anything but a letter or a space: W. The
                              STY   <AT   ;   place is that character, just read
                              LDA   #"W"   
                    EJMP:     JMP   error   ; (H and N come here too)
F171                          ENDIF      
F171   A6 A0        H_DEF:    LDA   ,Y+   
F173   80 41                  SUBA   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
F175   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ;   lands 64 bytes up
F177   C4 DF                  ANDB   #0DFh   ; fold case
F179   C1 1A                  CMPB   #26   
F17B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F17B   24 0A                  BHS   def2   ; not a letter
F17D                          ENDIF      
F17D                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BHS   def1   
F17D                          ENDIF      
F17D   BD F0 75               JSR   cellx   
F180   1F 20                  TFR   Y,D   
F182   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; little-endian
F184   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F186   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the PSHU)
F187   36 20        DEF2:     PSHU   Y   ; an anonymous block: push its address
F189                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F189                             ; fall into skip
F189                          ENDIF      
F189                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Checked: the skip must end at a "]" (A = 2), or for a false "(",
                                 ; which comes to opf, at a ")" (A = 0). Anything else stops with N.
                              BSR   skip   
                              SUBA   #2   
                              FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the BSR)
                    OPF:      BSR   skip   
                              TSTA      
                              BEQ   sk9   ; (an RTS)
                              LDA   #"N"   
                              BRA   ejmp   
F189                          ENDIF      
F189                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
F189                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
F189                             ; strings are stepped over whole. B counts the open levels.
F189                             ; Unchecked: a NUL first ends the program (for "\" with no closer; anything
F189                             ; else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets anyway).
F189                             ; Checked: a NUL, or a string that runs into it, returns A = FFh, and the
F189                             ; caller decides: "\" ends the program, "(" and "[" stop with N, as they do
F189                             ; for a closer of the other kind. The place is the opener, still in AT.
F189   5F           SKIP:     CLRB      
F18A   A6 A0        SK1:      LDA   ,Y+   
F18C                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F18C   10 27 FE E2            LBEQ   fin   
F190                          ENDIF      
F190                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   ssn   ; A = FFh
F190                          ENDIF      
F190   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F192   26 02                  BNE   sk2   
F194   8D 79                  BSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
F196                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BCS   sk9   ; (or FFh, with the carry set: unclosed)
F196                          ENDIF      
F196   80 28        SK2:      SUBA   #"("   
F198   27 0F                  BEQ   sk3   
F19A   4A                     DECA      ; ")"
F19B   27 08                  BEQ   sk4   
F19D   80 32                  SUBA   #"["-")"   
F19F   27 08                  BEQ   sk3   
F1A1   81 02                  CMPA   #"]"-"["   
F1A3   26 E5                  BNE   sk1   
F1A5   5A           SK4:      DECB      
F1A6   2A E2                  BPL   sk1   
F1A8   39           SK9:      RTS      ; the closer at this level
F1A9   5C           SK3:      INCB      
F1AA   20 DE                  BRA   sk1   
F1AC                             ; 22h, checked build (the unchecked one is with the handlers below).
F1AC                             ; Checked: a NUL ends the string too, even right after a "/"; skipstr then
F1AC                             ; returns A = FFh with the carry set (the carry is clear at the quote), and
F1AC                             ; """ stops with Q, the string's address already pushed. (skip comes here
F1AC                             ; for its own NUL as well.)
F1AC                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
                              BSR   skipstr   
                              LBCS   e_quote   
                              RTS      
                    SS0:      LDA   ,Y+   ; the character after the "/"
                              BEQ   ssn   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
                              BEQ   ssn   
                              CMPA   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMPA   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      ; the quote: C = 0
                    SSN:      SUBA   #1   ; the NUL: A = FFh, C = 1
                              RTS      
F1AC                          ENDIF      
F1AC   AE C4        H_FETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; "@" (the cell in memory is little-endian)
F1AE   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F1B0   20 6B                  BRA   cf1   
F1B2                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
F1B2                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
F1B2                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
F1B2                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
F1B2                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
F1B2   AE C4        H_KEY:    LDX   ,U   
F1B4   2B 17                  BMI   line   
F1B6   C6 14        KT1:      LDB   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
F1B8   BD F0 AD     KT2:      JSR   getk   
F1BB   26 0B                  BNE   kt3   
F1BD   5A                     DECB      
F1BE   26 F8                  BNE   kt2   
F1C0   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F1C2   26 F2                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
F1C4   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   ; 0?: the countdown from 0 took 65536 ms;
F1C6   27 EE                  BEQ   kt1   ;   run it again, until a key comes
F1C8   6F C4        KT3:      CLR   ,U   
F1CA   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F1CC   39                     RTS      
F1CD                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
F1CD                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
F1CD                             ; is full. B = the length so far; the low byte of the top cell becomes the
F1CD                             ; most allowed (it holds minus the count on entry).
F1CD   8C FF 81     LINE:     CMPX   #-127   ; (X = TOS, minus the count)
F1D0   24 04                  BHS   ln1   
F1D2   86 81                  LDA   #-127   ; more than 127 is taken as 127
F1D4   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F1D6   60 41        LN1:      NEG   1,U   
F1D8   8E 82 80               LDX   #LINEBUF   
F1DB   5F                     CLRB      
F1DC   BD F0 AD     LN2:      JSR   getk   
F1DF   27 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
F1E1   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F1E3   27 16                  BEQ   ln5   
F1E5   81 08                  CMPA   #8   
F1E7   27 0C                  BEQ   ln4   
F1E9   E1 41                  CMPB   1,U   
F1EB   24 EF                  BHS   ln2   ; full
F1ED   A7 85                  STA   B,X   
F1EF   5C                     INCB      
F1F0   BD FF 03     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
F1F3   20 E7                  BRA   ln2   
F1F5   5D           LN4:      TSTB      ; Backspace: nothing to take back?
F1F6   27 E4                  BEQ   ln2   
F1F8   5A                     DECB      
F1F9   20 F5                  BRA   ln3   ; echo it
F1FB   A7 85        LN5:      STA   B,X   ; A = 13
F1FD   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F1FF   39                     RTS      
F200                             ; =============================================================================
F200                             ;  Handlers that must start in the second range (unchecked build).
F200                             ; =============================================================================
F200                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
F200                             ; the matching ")".
F200   EC C1        H_OPEN:   LDD   ,U++   
F202                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F202   27 85                  BEQ   skip   ; tail call: skip ends in RTS
F204                          ENDIF      
F204                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBEQ   opf   ; checked: skip, and check the closer
F204                          ENDIF      
F204   35 10                  PULS   X   
F206   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F208   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F20A                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
F20A                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
F20A                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h. (The checked
F20A                             ; build's is after skip.)
F20A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F20A   36 20        H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
F20C   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAY)
F20D   31 21        SS0:      LEAY   1,Y   
F20F   A6 A0        SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
F211   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F213   27 F8                  BEQ   ss0   
F215   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F217   26 F6                  BNE   skipstr   
F219   39                     RTS      
F21A                          ENDIF      
F21A   AE C4        H_CFETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; ","
F21C   4F                     CLRA      
F21D   E6 84        CF1:      LDB   ,X   
F21F   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F221   39                     RTS      
F222                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
F222                             ; drops it and carries on.
F222   EC C1        H_CLOSE:   LDD   ,U++   
F224   10 27 FF 45            LBEQ   rdrop   
F228   10 AE 62               LDY   2,S   ; the block start, under the return address
F22B   7E F0 A0               JMP   pollk   ; the break check, at every loop-back
F22E                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
F22E                             ; "*": three 8x8 multiplies; only the low 16 bits are kept.
F22E                             ; a = ah:al at 2,U.  b = bh:bl at ,U.
F22E   A6 43        H_MUL:    LDA   3,U   
F230   E6 C4                  LDB   ,U   
F232   3D                     MUL      ; al*bh
F233   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; (bh is no longer needed)
F235   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F237   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F239   3D                     MUL      ; ah*bl
F23A   EB C4                  ADDB   ,U   
F23C   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; the cross terms, low byte
F23E   A6 43                  LDA   3,U   
F240   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F242   3D                     MUL      ; al*bl
F243   AB C4                  ADDA   ,U   
F245   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F247   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F249   39                     RTS      
F24A                             ; Signed compares: a-b, then a branch to put -1 or 0 on the stack.
F24A   8D 18        H_GT:     BSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
F24C   8D 10        H_LT:     BSR   cmp   
F24E   2D 02                  BLT   true   
F250   5F           FALSE:    CLRB      
F251   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDB)
F252   C6 FF        TRUE:     LDB   #0FFh   
F254   1D                     SEX      ; D = 0000 or FFFF
F255   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F257   39                     RTS      
F258   8D 04        H_EQ:     BSR   cmp   
F25A   27 F6                  BEQ   true   
F25C   20 F2                  BRA   false   
F25E   EC 42        CMP:      LDD   2,U   
F260   10 A3 C1               CMPD   ,U++   
F263   39                     RTS      
F264                             ; ---- stack, and printing ----------------------------------------------------
F264   37 16        H_SWAP:   PULU   D,X   ; "%"
F266   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F268   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F26A   39                     RTS      
F26B   EC C4        H_DUP:    LDD   ,U   ; ":"
F26D   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F26F   39                     RTS      
F270   A6 41        H_EMIT:   LDA   1,U   ; "'"
F272                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F272   8D 4C                  BSR   putc   
F274                          ENDIF      
F274                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   CONOUT   ; (the checked build's report is in the way)
F274                          ENDIF      
F274   33 42        H_DROP:   LEAU   2,U   ; ";"
F276   39                     RTS      
F277                             ; ---- more arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------------
F277   EC C1        H_AND:    LDD   ,U++   
F279   A4 C4                  ANDA   ,U   
F27B   E4 41                  ANDB   1,U   
F27D   20 04                  BRA   st   
F27F   EC C1        H_ADD:    LDD   ,U++   
F281   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F283   ED C4        ST:       STD   ,U   
F285   39                     RTS      
F286                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
F286                             ; (The checked build has it in the tail, near negnum: its report would be
F286                             ; in the way here.)
F286                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F286   BD F0 7C     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
F289   25 7C                  BLO   negnum   
F28B   EC 42                  LDD   2,U   
F28D   A3 C1                  SUBD   ,U++   
F28F   20 F2                  BRA   st   
F291                          ENDIF      
F291                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." with the high byte stored first. The cell in
F291                             ; memory is little-endian.
F291                             ; Checked: both bytes must be in the program's space, and they are tested
F291                             ; before either is stored (chkst stops with O, the stack untouched).
F291                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F291   37 10        H_STORE:   PULU   X   
F293   A6 C4                  LDA   ,U   
F295   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F297                          ENDIF      
F297                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_STORE:   LDX   ,U   
                              BSR   chkst   
                              LEAX   1,X   
                              BSR   chkst   
                              LDA   2,U   
                              STA   ,X   
                                 ; and fall into ".", which loads X again (and checks it again)
F297                          ENDIF      
F297                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F297   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the PULU)
F298   37 10        H_CSTORE:   PULU   X   ; "." ( c addr -- )
F29A                          ENDIF      
F29A                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_CSTORE:   LDX   ,U   ; "." ( c addr -- )
                              BSR   chkst   
                              LEAU   2,U   
F29A                          ENDIF      
F29A   37 06                  PULU   D   
F29C   E7 84                  STB   ,X   
F29E   39                     RTS      
F29F                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; ---- reached from a handler ------------------------------------------------
                                 ; chkst: stop with O unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter
                                 ; page up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
                                 ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
                                 ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
                    CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
                              BLO   cs9   
                              CMPX   #HEAPLIM*256   
                              BHS   cs9   
                              RTS      ; in range
                    CS9:      LDA   #"O"   
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; / by zero
                              FCB   8Ch   
                    E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; " or $ ran into the NUL
                                 ; and fall into error. (H, W and N have their own entries, near
                                 ; their handlers, at ejmp.)
                                 ; =============================================================================
                                 ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
                                 ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
                                 ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
                                 ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
                                 ;  short calls. Prints
                                 ; 
                                 ;     CR LF
                                 ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
                                 ;     <up to 16 raw characters from the place, ending early at CR, LF, NUL>
                                 ;     CR LF
                                 ;     Stk n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
                                 ;     Rtn n CR LF
                                 ; 
                                 ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
                                 ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
                                 ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
                                 ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
                                 ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
                                 ; 
                                 ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 80FEh): the
                                 ;  report's own cells then reach 8 bytes further down, to 80F6h, into the
                                 ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
                                 ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
                                 ; =============================================================================
                    ERROR:    LDS   #RSREP   
                              TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
                              TFR   B,A   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   " @"," "+80h   
                                 ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
                                 ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
                              LDY   #0   
                              LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
                              PSHU   X   
                              LDX   #PROG-1   
                              CMPX   <AT   
                              BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
                              STX   ,U   
                    LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
                    LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
                              CMPX   <AT   
                              BHS   lc3   
                              LDA   ,X   
                              CMPA   #10   
                              BNE   lc2   
                              STX   ,U   
                              BRA   lc1   
                                 ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
                                 ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
                                 ; (It sits here, in the middle of the report, where all its calls reach.)
                    PMSG:     PULS   X   
                    PM1:      LDA   ,X   
                              ANDA   #7Fh   
                              JSR   putc   
                              TST   ,X+   
                              BPL   pm1   
                              JMP   ,X   
                    LC3:      LDD   <AT   
                              SUBD   ,U   
                              STD   ,U   ; the column
                              PSHU   Y   
                              BSR   pdec   ; the line
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   ","+80h   
                              BSR   pdec   ; the column
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10+80h   
                                 ; the text at the place
                              LDX   <AT   
                              LDB   #16   
                    TX1:      LDA   ,X+   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              CMPA   #10   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              CMPA   #13   
                              BEQ   tx9   
                              BSR   putc   
                              DECB      
                              BNE   tx1   
                    TX9:      BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
                                 ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
                                 ; the program's top cell, at ,U.
                              PSHS   U   ; where the walk ends
                              LDD   #DSTOP   
                              SUBD   ,S   
                              BSR   pdh   ; the depth (pdec leaves U as it was)
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   ":"+80h   
                              LEAY   16,U   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
                              CMPY   #DSTOP   
                              BHS   sl1   
                              BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
                              FCB   " ..","."+80h   
                              BRA   sl2   
                    SL1:      LDY   #DSTOP   ; ... or the whole stack, if no more than 8
                    SL2:      CMPY   ,S   
                              BLS   sl9   
                              LDD   ,--Y   
                              PSHU   D   
                              BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   " "+80h   
                              BSR   h_num   
                              BRA   sl2   
                    SL9:      BSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
                              LDD   #RSTOP   ; the return stack's depth, (RSTOP - S) / 2,
                              SUBD   <SSAV   ;   S as it was when this character began
                              BSR   pdh   
                              JSR   pmsg   
                              FCB   13,10+80h   
                              JMP   EXIT   
                                 ; pdh: print D/2 (a depth: D is twice it), unsigned.
                    PDH:      LSRA      
                              RORB      
                              PSHU   D   
                              BRA   pdec   
F29F                          ENDIF      
F29F                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F29F   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F2A1   2A 06                  BPL   pdec   
F2A3   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F2A5   8D 19                  BSR   putc   
F2A7   8D 61                  BSR   negt   
F2A9                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F2A9   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F2AC   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F2AE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
F2AE   8D 69                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F2B0                          ENDIF      
F2B0                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LBSR   udiv   ; (out of a BSR's reach here)
F2B0                          ENDIF      
F2B0   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F2B2   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F2B4   EC C1                  LDD   ,U++   ; the quotient: if it is not 0, it goes
F2B6   27 04                  BEQ   pd1   ;   back for the rest of the digits
F2B8   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F2BA   8D ED                  BSR   pdec   
F2BC   35 02        PD1:      PULS   A   
F2BE   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F2C0   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F2C3                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F2C3                             ; "$" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F2C3                             ; second range: its loop, the escapes, and the routines of "/".
F2C3                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F2C3                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F2C3                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
F2C3                             ; it stops with Z, both operands still on the stack.
F2C3                H_DIV:       
F2C3                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDD   ,U   
                              LBEQ   e_zero   
F2C3                          ENDIF      
F2C3   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F2C5   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F2C7   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F2C9   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F2CB   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F2CD   8D 44                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F2CF   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F2D1   8D 40                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F2D3   8D 44                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F2D5   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F2D7   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F2D9   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F2DB   8D 2F                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F2DD   6D E0        DV1:      TST   ,S+   
F2DF   2A 31                  BPL   ng9   
F2E1   20 27                  BRA   negt   ; r's sign
F2E3                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
F2E3                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
F2E3                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /? is DEL"s "?"; "/" and """ have
F2E3                             ; no bit 6, so // and /" give themselves). The address comes off the stack
F2E3                             ; first, and Y walks the string (the IP waits on S), so that /~ finds its
F2E3                             ; row and column on top, and an escape may use A, B, X and the routines.
F2E3                             ; Checked: a NUL (not one escaped by "/") stops with Q, the string's
F2E3                             ; address put back on the stack (from PSAV) over what any /~ left.
F2E3   34 20        H_PRINT:   PSHS   Y   
F2E5   37 20                  PULU   Y   
F2E7                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STY   <PSAV   
F2E7                          ENDIF      
F2E7   A6 A0        PR0:      LDA   ,Y+   
F2E9                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   prq   
F2E9                          ENDIF      
F2E9   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F2EB   27 18                  BEQ   pr9   
F2ED   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F2EF   26 10                  BNE   pr1   
F2F1   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F2F3   80 60                  SUBA   #60h   ; ` 0, a-z 1-26, 00bbIDI3LCB8IDI4LCA= 29, ~ 30
F2F5   81 1F                  CMPA   #1Fh   
F2F7   24 04                  BHS   pr2   
F2F9   8D 47                  BSR   pesc   
F2FB   20 EA                  BRA   pr0   
F2FD   8B 60        PR2:      ADDA   #60h   ; any other: bit 6 goes
F2FF   84 BF                  ANDA   #0BFh   
F301   8D BD        PR1:      BSR   putc   
F303   20 E2                  BRA   pr0   
F305   35 A0        PR9:      PULS   Y,PC   
F307                          IF   CHECKED   
                    PRQ:      LDX   <PSAV   
                              PSHU   X   
                              JMP   e_quote   
F307                          ENDIF      
F307                             ; "-", checked build (see the unchecked one, before "!").
F307                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
                              BLO   negnum   
                              LDD   2,U   
                              SUBD   ,U++   
                              BRA   ud3   ; (STD ,U / RTS)
F307                          ENDIF      
F307   BD F0 83     NEGNUM:   JSR   rdnum   ; a negative literal: read it, then negate
F30A   1F 31        NEGT:     TFR   U,X   
F30C   4F           NEGX:     CLRA      ; negx: negate the cell at X
F30D   5F                     CLRB      
F30E   A3 84                  SUBD   ,X   
F310   ED 84                  STD   ,X   
F312   39           NG9:      RTS      
F313   6D 84        ABSX:     TST   ,X   ; absx: negate the cell at X if negative
F315   2A FB                  BPL   ng9   
F317   20 F3                  BRA   negx   
F319                             ; udiv: unsigned divide, in place. The dividend is the NOS cell and the
F319                             ; divisor the TOS cell, both <= 8000h; the NOS cell becomes the quotient and
F319                             ; the TOS cell the remainder. The remainder is built in D (always < the
F319                             ; divisor, so 2R+1 fits in 16 bits).
F319                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
F319   EC C4        UDIV:     LDD   ,U   
F31B   83 00 02               SUBD   #2   
F31E   26 07                  BNE   ud0   
F320   64 42                  LSR   2,U   
F322   66 43                  ROR   3,U   ; the quotient
F324   59                     ROLB      ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D was 0)
F325   20 18                  BRA   ud3   
F327   8E 00 10     UD0:      LDX   #16   
F32A   4F                     CLRA      
F32B   5F                     CLRB      
F32C   68 43        UD1:      ASL   3,U   
F32E   69 42                  ROL   2,U   ; the dividend's top bit ...
F330   59                     ROLB      
F331   49                     ROLA      ; ... into the remainder
F332   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   
F335   25 04                  BLO   ud2   
F337   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F339   6C 43                  INC   3,U   ; a quotient bit
F33B   30 1F        UD2:      LEAX   -1,X   
F33D   26 ED                  BNE   ud1   
F33F   ED C4        UD3:      STD   ,U   
F341   39                     RTS      
F342                             ; pesc: the escapes of "$". A = the character after the "/", minus 60h
F342                             ; (0 to 30); Y points past it. Each returns to the loop with an RTS, its
F342                             ; own or that of the routine it ends by jumping to. A, B and X are free.
F342                             ;    /a-/z   print the variable, as "#" does
F342                             ;    /{      clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
F342                             ;    /}      clear from the cursor to the end of the line
F342                             ;    /|  /`  show the cursor, hide it
F342                             ;    /~      ( row col -- ) the cursor to that row and column, from 0
F342   81 1B        PESC:     CMPA   #27   
F344   24 29                  BHS   pcon   
F346   48                     ASLA      ; (` leaves A = 0: hide)
F347   27 35                  BEQ   phide   
F349   8E 82 3E               LDX   #LET+40h-2   ; the variable's cell (little-endian)
F34C   EC 86                  LDD   A,X   
F34E   1E 89                  EXG   A,B   
F350   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F352   7E F2 9F               JMP   h_num   
